Template: show-folder-size-nautilus/cache-dir
Type: string
Default: ~/.cache/show-folder-size-nautilus
Description: Where should folder sizes be cached?
 The Total Size column remembers measured folder sizes so re-visiting a
 folder is instant instead of re-measuring it. This sets the system-wide
 default location for that cache.
 .
 A leading ~/ is expanded per user, so the default gives every user their
 own cache under their home directory. An absolute path shared between
 users is possible but rarely what you want.
 .
 Leave this empty to disable on-disk caching entirely: sizes are then
 remembered only until nautilus restarts, and the extension writes nothing
 to disk at all.
 .
 Individual users can override this in ~/.config/show-folder-size-nautilus.conf.
